<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Kerman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1794">1794</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as final siege at Kerman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a> was the final siege in 1794 in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> leader Agha Mohammad Khan captured the city of Kerman from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lotf-ali-khan">Lotf Ali Khan</a>, the last Zand ruler. The city's inhabitants were punished by mass blinding. Lotf Ali Khan was captured and tortured to death, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-kerman.jpg" alt="Siege of Kerman" width="264" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Capture_and_Sack_of_Kerman_by_Agha_Mohammad_Khan_Qajar.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
